1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:24,660
kick a whetstone and
even your shoes go flying.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Will you take notice of me, I wonder?

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
They laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow summon some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
pachinko, sighs, yawns,
nothing ever changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat,
from the purification fountain,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset sinks into the vast sky.

10
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too, it all ends like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,720
Happiness, they say,
in Katsushika and Shibamata.

12
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:24,480
Dizzy with it all,
I realized I'm just a fool.

13
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:38,400
Happy Birthday to you

14
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,940
Happy Birthday to you

15
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:47,720
Happy Birthday dear Honda-chan

16
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,120
BIRTHDAY TO YOU

17
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,800
Happy birthday!

18
00:01:55,340 --> 00:02:00,220
Hehehe, alright, blow them all out at once!

19
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:00,740
Phew

20
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:04,280
Ugh, fine, like this, see?

21
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:08,260
Phew, hehe, congratulations.

22
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:13,420
Throwing such a grand party for me,

23
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,940
Uuuuuuu

24
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:17,900
There's no need to cry.

25
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:21,700
I'm feeling a little embarrassed, you know.

26
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:26,360
His birthday has become his
183rd heartbreak anniversary.

27
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:28,380
Well, it can't be helped.

28
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,960
Poor Honda-san.

29
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,780
Uuuuuuu...

30
00:02:31,780 --> 00:02:33,700
So which woman was it this time?

31
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,260
It's the convenience store girl.

32
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,760
It's about what happened
this morning, though.

33
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:43,320
Aaaaah!
We're one minute from being late, hurry, go!

34
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:46,780
I'm just going to stop by somewhere on the way,
Mr. Yoshizuka.

35
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:52,540
Whoa!

36
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:53,860
That's awful!

37
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:56,240
What the heck!

38
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,900
Can I really accept something like this?

39
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:06,960
Don't mind it, Midori.
Love rings are common knowledge now, right?

40
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,360
I'm happy!

41
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:15,920
You, b-, don't tell me you
like that girl from just now...

42
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:23,940
Midori-chan's burger!

43
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,620
Honda-san, you're really pitiful.

44
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:36,920
Wuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

45
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,200
Why does it always have
to be me who gets dumped?

46
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,000
You're just trying to get into the Guinness Book,
aren't you?

47
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,700
Hey, don't say that.

48
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:44,660
Hey!

49
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:46,080
You mustn't.

50
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:48,260
It's fine. I don't care what happens to me.

51
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,760
Senpai, please stop with the bad jokes.

52
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:52,780
Well, that's easy for you to say.

53
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,640
Here you go, Honda-san.

54
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,340
This is a birthday present
from Kei-chan and me.

55
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:01,100
This should cheer you up.

56
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:06,660
Isn't that the new model helmet?

57
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,420
How touching.

58
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,180
Good for you, Honda.

59
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:12,360
Yes, thank you very much.

60
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,660
I'm glad he likes it, Reiko-san.

61
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:18,400
Yes, with this, I'll blow that
heartbreak right out of my mind.

62
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:19,520
Heartbreak?

63
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,160
Heartbreak

64
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:25,840
Idiot, I was just about to forget it.

65
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,040
Sorry, Honda-san.

66
00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:31,100
What I meant was,
I hope you find a new girlfriend with this.

67
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:31,560
Yeah.

68
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,100
That's right.

69
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:35,460
There are as many women as
there are stars in the sky.

70
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:38,940
Put this on and start talking to girls,
and you'll have your pick of the lot.

71
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:39,600
Midori.

72
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:41,940
Midori.

73
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:43,500
You idiot!

74
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,600
Her name was Midori, the girl who dumped me.

75
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,260
Sorry.

76
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:50,300
Honda-sama, here's our present for you.

77
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:51,260
Yeah, that's right.

78
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:54,500
Honda, we don't have as much
money as Reiko and the others,

79
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,160
so it's nothing special, but...

80
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:57,160
Here.

81
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,980
A helmet?

82
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:04,440
We even prayed that you'd get
a girlfriend as good as this!

83
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,020
Isn't that nice?

84
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:08,180
It's really heartfelt, isn't it?

85
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:10,860
Thank you, senpai, Maria-san.

86
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:14,240
We'll put them on your bike and helmet.

87
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:15,962
Thank goodness, Ryo-sama,

88
00:05:16,012 --> 00:05:19,380
our prayers together to
the gods paid off after all.

89
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:24,680
I also prayed that I could
become lovey-dovey with Ryo-sama.

90
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:54,300
Lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey,
lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey, lovey-dovey.

91
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,960
Once we're sure,
we'll look for a cute girl for you.

92
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,400
Really?

93
00:05:58,620 --> 00:05:58,980
Yes.

94
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,120
Please do.

95
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:01,380
Please do.

96
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:02,480
Please do.

97
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:03,380
Please do.

98
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,160
Please do.

99
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:05,520
Honda!

100
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,380
What's with that servile attitude?

101
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:12,260
Yo-chan, he was finally in a good mood.

102
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:12,580
Shut up!

103
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:15,840
That's like wrestling sumo
in someone else's loincloth.

104
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:21,320
Honda, if you change how you live when you're not riding your bike,
you'll get a girlfriend in no time.

105
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:23,440
Change how I live?

106
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:26,861
This, and that,

107
00:06:26,911 --> 00:06:29,400
and that too. Is this a guy's room?

108
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:32,680
It really does look like a girl's room.

109
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:36,900
The books lined up on the shelf are all shoujo manga,
after all.

110
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:41,240
I can't believe this is the room
of someone feared as a demon.

111
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,640
Right? So first of all...

112
00:06:45,280 --> 00:06:47,320
W-what are you doing, senpai?!

113
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:49,200
We're throwing all of this junk away.

114
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:52,351
Stop it! My treasures,

115
00:06:52,401 --> 00:06:54,040
Miko-sensei of Love's...

116
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,980
If I say I'm throwing it away,
I'm throwing it away!

117
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:58,680
Noooo!

118
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:04,900
Thank goodness!

119
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,500
Honda!

120
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,440
You really did it, Honda!

121
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,420
No, senpai, it's a misunderstanding!
A misunderstanding!

122
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,380
I don't want to hear any excuses!

123
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,280
Hey, Ryo-chan!

124
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,200
The cake! The cake!

125
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,380
What happened?

126
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:19,980
Aaaaaah!

127
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:25,780
Well, the birthday party's ruined,
what a waste.

128
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:32,000
I'm sorry, Ryo-sama. It was my fault for saying something unnecessary.
You don't need to apologize, Maria-chan.

129
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,340
It's Ryo-chan's fault, so shut up!

130
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,740
Hey, how's it going?

131
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:39,840
Yeah!

132
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:42,360
Y-yeah, yeah!

133
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:46,220
Senpai, I'm sorry about yesterday.

134
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:47,720
Listen, you...

135
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,380
Father

136
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,175
Honda-san,

137
00:07:49,225 --> 00:07:52,440
I got my hands on a list of singles in the prefecture.
Want to see?

138
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,380
No, I'm good.

139
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:58,340
Honda, don't tell me you've
got another crush on some girl?

140
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:02,160
You're so sharp,
I can't hide anything from you.

141
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,880
Y-you've already bounced back?

142
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,360
Didn't I tell you before?

143
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:10,060
He sulks fast, but he recovers even faster.

144
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,380
So which girl is it this time?

145
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:14,780
Well, I'm, like, a former Tokyo
University resident, so to speak.

146
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:21,020
A super-cute new officer just
joined our 4th Traffic Mobile Unit.

147
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:23,360
You mean the new recruit, Olive-chan?

148
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,300
You know her?

149
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,460
Olive.

150
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:33,560
She only weighs 35 kilos and is as thin as a twig,
so everyone calls her Olive.

151
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:34,560
Olive

152
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:35,020
Yes.

153
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:35,600
Alright.

154
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:36,960
Well then, shall we go?

155
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,300
H-hold on, senpai!

156
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:41,180
You're going to confess
your love to that Olive-chan.

157
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,960
Right now?

158
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:45,860
Better to settle it while
the wound is still shallow.

159
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:46,900
N-no way...

160
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,660
Ryo-chan, you're so pushy!

161
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,860
It just shows how much
he cares about his friend.

162
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:53,260
I don't want to get shot down.

163
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:54,740
Alright, follow me.

164
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:55,700
Senpai...

165
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:04,700
Olive-chan, her real name is Nana Otohime.

166
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,540
She's practically a teenager, isn't she?

167
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,760
You're so slender. Like glasswork.

168
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:12,060
That's why they call her Olive-chan.

169
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:13,400
Hey, you!

170
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,520
Are you talking to me?

171
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,640
Whoa, you've got such an anime voice.

172
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:21,640
I get told that a lot. Sorry.

173
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,760
No need to apologize.
It's cute and suits you.

174
00:09:26,240 --> 00:09:29,820
Anyway, Honda wants to go out with you.

175
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:31,440
Honda-san?

176
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,000
Honda from the police box, you know.

177
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,660
You said Olive-chan was cool, didn't you?

178
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,240
But Honda-chan is

179
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:40,620
the one with the scary face
who yells right away, right?

180
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:42,120
Yes, that's the one.

181
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,980
Come on, lean the bike over more!

182
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:46,560
What the hell, I'll do it!

183
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:48,140
Pull yourself together!

184
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,160
That's actually me.

185
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:52,820
But your face...

186
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:56,260
He's quiet usually, but his
personality changes when he rides a bike.

187
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,140
Really?

188
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:59,140
Seeing is believing.

189
00:09:59,140 --> 00:09:59,560
That.

190
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,460
He really is that instructor.

191
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:13,440
Think of him as Jekyll and Hyde.

192
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:18,460
Do you understand now?

193
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:19,380
Y-yes.

194
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:22,700
Hey, Olive-chan,
won't you go out with this guy?

195
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,560
With the instructor?

196
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:28,180
S-senpai,
it looks like it's hopeless after all.

197
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:29,120
Oh yeah?

198
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:32,100
Olive-chan, are you seeing anyone right now?

199
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:33,180
Wh-wait a minute.

200
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,240
No one's here.

201
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:38,020
That's perfect! Go out with Honda.

202
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:39,060
Senpai.

203
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:48,620
Yes, nice to meet you.

204
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:51,740
Yes! It's a total success!

205
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:55,700
Senpai, this isn't a dream, right?

206
00:10:55,700 --> 00:10:58,080
Please pinch my cheek.

207
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,440
Alright!

208
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,880
Good for you, Honda.

209
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:18,800
I never knew my life could
bring me such good luck.

210
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:22,500
Honda Hayato!

211
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:27,080
I have no regrets in my life.

212
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:02,500
Oh no.

213
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,880
It's the later-era Honda!

214
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:06,220
That demon Honda?

215
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:08,300
Slow down a bit!

216
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:09,460
Here,

217
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:11,340
here!

218
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:17,540
Yo, Honda-san!

219
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:20,620
What are you lot dawdling for?

220
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,980
If you're bōsōzoku, ride harder!

221
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:27,400
Huh? Is that really okay?

222
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,120
I permit it!

223
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:33,140
Go on, everyone! Now is the time of youth!

224
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,420
Cut through the wind! Fall in love!

225
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,840
Love is wonderful!

226
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,860
Gleam Shot!

227
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:47,620
What's going on here?

228
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:49,900
Isn't this super dangerous?
Maybe there's an earthquake or something?

229
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:55,660
What are you doing, Honda?

230
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:58,920
Hey, senpai,
I was thinking of throwing out my comics.

231
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,079
I see,

232
00:13:00,129 --> 00:13:03,920
So the power of love has
finally changed Honda's lifestyle

233
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:07,780
Real romance beats shojo manga romance,
after all.

234
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:10,000
Look at him, gushing about it.

235
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,760
Alright, I'll help you out too.

236
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,240
Not that one, that's no good.

237
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,520
Why not?

238
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:19,461
Ai no Miko-sensei has been a huge fan since the Lidio days,
so

239
00:13:19,511 --> 00:13:20,900
I want to keep them.

240
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:23,860
Well, this much should be fine.

241
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:33,660
Yes, that's proof that Honda is getting along well with Olive,
isn't it?

242
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:36,120
He's been acting so cocky every day.

243
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:38,580
Nakagawa, shall we take a quick look?

244
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,400
Yeah, sure.

245
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:48,700
Instructor, please help me!

246
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:54,480
What happened? What are you doing out here?

247
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,523
It's just that my tire
got stuck in the ditch,

248
00:13:58,573 --> 00:14:00,500
and no matter what I do, it won't budge.

249
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:03,560
Hey, you think you've got it rough? You're in the second half of your training,
aren't you?

250
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,120
Sorry!

251
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,980
In situations like this,
you use the suspension.

252
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,260
Anyway, it's dangerous, so get on the bike.

253
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:11,960
Y-yes!

254
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:14,080
Sink the front suspension!

255
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:14,740
Yes!

256
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,500
Use the handlebars and
pull it out in one go!

257
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:17,180
Yes!

258
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:18,620
It's out!

259
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:19,920
Once it's out, brake!

260
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:22,540
That was a beautiful bit of riding,
Nakagawa.

261
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:24,480
Same technique:
sink the suspension and come on over!

262
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:28,020
Spring has finally come for Honda too, but

263
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:29,720
Turn the handlebars and change direction.

264
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,400
Yes.

265
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:37,740
Instructor, thank you so much for today.

266
00:14:38,640 --> 00:14:41,280
Good work, you've gotten so much better.

267
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,880
Olive-chan.

268
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:46,380
It's because the instructor teaches so well,
I'm sure.

269
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,300
I like the instructor when riding that bike,

270
00:14:50,300 --> 00:14:52,640
but I also love the
instructor when getting off.

271
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:55,900
No, come on.

272
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,700
Well, excuse me.

273
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:58,960
Olive-chan.

274
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,120
Yes?

275
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:04,000
This coming Sunday,

276
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:07,920
how about we go see a movie together?

277
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:09,960
Sunday?

278
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,700
Well, only if you're free, but how about it?

279
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,540
I'm sorry.

280
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:20,820
I'm sorry, even though you invited me.

281
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:23,220
But, well then...

282
00:15:32,020 --> 00:15:33,120
I'm sorry.

283
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:36,300
It was my fault for not listening to you.

284
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:37,640
Yoshiko-chan

285
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:47,040
I was really supposed to
watch it with Olive-chan.

286
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:51,760
Please be quiet.

287
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,180
Sorry, sorry.

288
00:15:55,180 --> 00:15:57,820
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

289
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:04,340
That was pretty good, wasn't it?

290
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:08,720
But you were asleep the whole time, Senpai.

291
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,620
That's exactly why it was good.

292
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:12,400
I feel refreshed.

293
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:14,580
That's just how it is.

294
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:18,740
What's wrong?

295
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,820
Hey, wasn't that Olive-chan just now?

296
00:16:32,820 --> 00:16:33,320
No way.

297
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,580
It happens all the time, even with a boss.

298
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:39,300
There's no boss as cool as that, you know.

299
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:44,300
Olive-chan looked so happy with him.

300
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:47,580
Calm down,
it's too early to jump to conclusions.

301
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,680
It could be a brother, you know.

302
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:56,700
Right. Or maybe a father?
Don't be ridiculous.

303
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:09,480
Senpai,
they went into her apartment together!

304
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:13,480
It happens all the time.
They're probably just having tea.

305
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:16,400
"It happens all the time"? With a woman?

306
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:16,680
No way.

307
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:27,140
Senpai! It's not coming out at all!
It's not tea, you know!

308
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,680
Then he must be eating dinner or something.

309
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,280
No way!

310
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:32,320
It happens all the time.

311
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:39,860
Tea, senpai, senpai, senpai.

312
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:42,680
What time is it?

313
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,700
It's 4 a.m.

314
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:46,640
Tch.

315
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,220
Hahahaha.

316
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:53,760
Thanks, it was really good.

317
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:58,020
Ryu-san just wouldn't let me sleep,
you know.

318
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:01,280
Sorry, sorry. See you later.

319
00:18:02,460 --> 00:18:03,720
Take care.

320
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:11,340
S-senpai, is this really
something that happens all the time?

321
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,640
It happens all the time.

322
00:18:16,040 --> 00:18:16,920
Yay!

323
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,800
Yay!

324
